      "description": "Watch Rangers vs Hibernian highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. The Scottish Premiership landscape shifted on August 9, 2026 , as Rangers hosted Hibernian in a contest filled with tactical maneuvering and high-stakes pressure. Both clubs entered the match seeking to assert their dominance in what proved to be a physically demanding encounter at the heart of the season. Early Penalty Drama The match ignited early when the visitors found an opening in the 11th minute. A foul by Vanja Dragojevic earned him a yellow card and handed Hibernian a golden opportunity from the penalty spot. Josh Campbell stepped up and clinically converted the penalty in the 12th minute, silencing the home crowd. Rangers struggled to find their rhythm in the first half and were forced into a tactical adjustment in the 36th minute, bringing on Ryan Don Naderi for Youssef Chermiti to spark some creativity. Tactical Shifts and Second Half Intensity As the second half commenced, Rangers introduced Mohamed Diomande to stabilize the midfield. The intensity remained high, with Hibernian 's Ante Suto receiving a yellow card just after the restart. In a bold move to maintain their lead, the visitors made a triple substitution in the 57th minute, introducing Nathan Lowe , Callum Wright , and Jamie McGrath . This injection of fresh energy proved vital as the game entered its most chaotic phase. Late Twist and Stoppage-Time Winner The drama reached a fever pitch in the closing stages. In the 85th minute, an unfortunate own goal by Miguel Chaiwa looked to have saved a point for Rangers , leveling the score at 1-1. However, the visitors refused to settle for a draw. Deep into stoppage time at 90+3', Nathan Lowe turned provider for Callum Wright , who struck a decisive blow to restore the lead. The 1-2 victory for Hibernian was confirmed minutes later, marking a famous win on the road and leaving the hosts reflecting on a night of missed opportunities."
